ads/2026/09/fang-gbc-goo-king.png","text","mediaReviewed","Screenshot source reviewed","value","2026-10-20","image","gameplay","Creator-published gameplay image from the Game Boy Color release page.","src","/GameMap/media/learning/fang-fox-gbc-claude.webp","alt","Fang faces the crowned Goo King and slimes in the Game Boy Color edition, with health and level HUD.","https://tinybitadventures.com/games/fang-the-fox-gbc/","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","Creator-published screenshot","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)",[87],"Claude Code","Creator evidence",[92],"evidence","section",{"_58":93,"_25":94,"_95":96},"Read the explicit Claude Code and Opus credit","https://tinybitadventures.com/fang-the-fox-on-the-game-boy-color/","note","First-person creator account names Claude Code with Opus 5.5 and distinguishes generated implementation from the creator’s direction and music listening. Reported automated test totals were not independently reproduced.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[101],{"_58":102,"_25":103,"_95":104},"Open the complete cartridge and browser project","https://github.com/TinyBitAdventures/fang-the-fox","The gbc/ C project, generators, music arrangements and web emulator are public. Download the whole repository: gbc/tools/build.js reads ../js data and sprites. Rebuilding requires Node and GBDK-2020 4.5.0; the ready-made ROM needs neither. Code/pixel art are MIT; music is excluded from that license.","More ways to play",[108],"distribution",{"_58":109,"_25":110,"_95":111},"GitHub Releases · GBC","https://github.com/TinyBitAdventures/fang-the-fox/releases/tag/gbc-v1.0.0","Download — Game Boy Color ROM and GBC release ZIP. Requires a compatible emulator or cartridge device; the ROM was not executed in this review.","Access type","playable","demo","Play or run",[117],{"_58":118,"_25":76,"_95":119},"Play Fang the Fox for Game Boy Color","Click Start game, focus the emulator, then press Enter/X to start. Arrow keys move, attack and talk; X is A, Z is B, Enter pauses, and Shift shows the area. Hold keys briefly across emulator frames. The page also offers a 256 KB .gbc ROM for compatible emulators or hardware.","Game platform","Browser","Guide format","build log","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[127],{"_58":128,"_25":94,"_95":-7},"Read the creator’s Game Boy porting account","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[133,134,135,136],"Start the browser emulator, choose New Game and advance the opening dialogue with X.","Move, interact and inspect the pause map before comparing the cartridge edition with the original browser game.","Read the creator’s porting account and the C implementation under gbc/src/.","Clone the whole repository, then use Node and GBDK-2020 4.5.0 to rebuild through gbc/Makefile; the generator also reads the root JavaScript game data.","AI workflow / foundation context","Austin Ginder says Claude Code running Opus 5.5 ported his browser game to C. The creator provided direction and listened to the adapted music; the public build tools share maps, sprites and rules between the original and the cartridge version.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","2D","track","metadata","Engine","GBDK-2020 4.5 · C / hUGEDriver","engine","lead","2d","ai-assisted",[133,134,135,136],{"_58":128,"_25":94,"_17":169},{"_58":118,"_25":76,"_17":113,"_95":119},{"_58":102,"_25":103,"_167":168,"_95":104},{"_58":93,"_25":94,"_95":96},"resourceIds",[],[163],{"_164":109,"_25":110,"_17":165,"_95":166},"platform","download","Game Boy Color ROM and GBC release ZIP. Requires a compatible emulator or cartridge device; the ROM was not executed in this review.","scope","complete-project","build-log",{"_171":172},"documents",{"_173":174,"_175":176},"en",[178,182,183,184,181,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,202,203,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,21